1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
A million on a normal paycheck takes a hundred and four years.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,460
Unless one thing happens— and nope, not a raise.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:12,620
The middle full-time worker in America makes about twelve thirty-two a week, says the government.

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,840
Times fifty-two weeks, that's about sixty-four thousand dollars a year.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,220
Now say you save fifteen percent of it, which is about eight hundred dollars a month.

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,940
Hit like if you're already doing this math in your head.

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,680
If that money just sits in a jar, a million takes a hundred and four years.

8
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:34,560
That's two and a half careers. But even saving every dollar takes fifteen and a half years.

9
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,280
Send this to the friend who says they'll be a millionaire by thirty.

10
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:42,040
Here's the twist. Money that grows earns money on top of itself.

11
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,480
Say your savings grow seven percent a year. That's an assumption, not a promise.

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:51,040
Now the same eight hundred a month hits a million in about thirty-one years.

13
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:54,020
Follow if you want math they never print on paychecks.

14
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:58,140
And only about three hundred thousand of that million is money you put in.

15
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:02,280
The other seven hundred thousand is growth. The money did most of the work.

16
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,740
So what percent of your paycheck do you save? Just the number.

